# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  .env.example — every environment variable the server, start.sh and the
#  build read. Copy to .env (root, used by `npm start` / Docker) or set the
#  values on the App Runner service. Never commit a real .env.
#
#  Layout
#    PART 1  REQUIRED FOR AN INFORMATIONAL SITE  — what a brochure/contact site
#            needs. Everything an Orkosi customer repo should set is here.
#    PART 2  ADVANCED / SaaS MODULES             — inherited SaaS foundation
#            (billing, OAuth, teams, uploads, search, ...). Disabled by default
#            for templateType "informational"; leave unset unless you turn a
#            module on.
#    PART 3  BUILD-TIME AND TOOLING              — Webpack, e2e, dev scripts.
#
#  CI checks that every `process.env.X` read in server/src and scripts/ is
#  documented in this file, so keep keys here even when a module is off.
#  Dev setup: `npm run bootstrap-env` copies server/.env.example and
#  client/.env.example; `npm run generate-keys` fills JWT keys.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  PART 1 — REQUIRED FOR AN INFORMATIONAL SITE                              ║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

# ── Runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development                   # development | test | production
PORT=3001                              # 3001 in dev (webpack dev server proxies to it); App Runner sets 3000
# BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0                    # Interface to bind (default 0.0.0.0)
LOG_LEVEL=info                         # pino level: trace | debug | info | warn | error
# SERVICE_NAME=server                  # Logger service name

# ── Public URL and CORS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000          # Public origin (REQUIRED in production): CORS allow-list, email links, sitemap
# CORS_ORIGINS=                        # Extra allowed origins, comma-separated (scheme + host, no path)

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED in production. start.sh runs migrations against it once per boot.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/myapp_dev
# DB_POOL_MAX=10                       # Max pooled connections
# DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT=30000           # ms before an idle client is closed
# DB_POOL_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT=2000      # ms to wait for a pooled client
# DB_POOL_SSL=true                     # "false" disables SSL (local Postgres)
# DB_SSL_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=true      # "false" accepts self-signed certs
# DB_SSL_CA=                           # PEM CA certificate for the DB connection
# DB_CONNECT_ATTEMPTS=5                # Startup connect retries (exponential backoff)
# DB_CONNECT_BASE_DELAY_MS=1000        # First retry delay
# DB_CONNECT_MAX_DELAY_MS=8000         # Retry delay cap

# ── Boot policy (start.sh / server startup) ──────────────────────────────────
# ALLOW_MIGRATION_FAILURE=0            # 1 = boot even when a migration failed on a REACHABLE database.
#                                      #     Temporary operator override only (docs/RUNBOOK.md section 2).
# ALLOW_DEGRADED_BOOT=0                # 1 = in production, keep serving with db=disconnected instead of exiting.
# ALLOW_EPHEMERAL_STORAGE=0            # 1 = permit STORAGE_PROVIDER=local in production (files vanish on redeploy).
# SKIP_STARTUP_MIGRATIONS=             # Set to 1 by start.sh after it ran migrations; do not set by hand.
# SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=10000            # Grace period for in-flight requests on SIGTERM

# ── Contact form ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# POST /api/contact stores every submission in contact_submissions and emails
# a notification. Without an email provider the notification is only logged.
# CONTACT_NOTIFY_EMAIL=hello@yourdomain.com   # Where notifications go (default: EMAIL_FROM)
# CONTACT_RETENTION_DAYS=365           # Purge submissions older than N days (unset = keep forever)
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=                # Cloudflare Turnstile secret; enables server-side captcha verification

# ── Email (notifications, contact form, auth mails) ──────────────────────────
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=ses|smtp|resend|console   # Default: auto-detect from the keys below, console otherwise
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com    # Sender address (fallback for every adapter)
# SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@yourdomain.com # Shown in email templates
# Resend
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# RESEND_REPLY_TO=
# AWS SES (also the default AWS credentials for S3/CloudFront when those are on)
# AWS_REGION=eu-west-1
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# SES_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@yourdomain.com
# Generic SMTP
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_SECURE=false                    # true for port 465 (implicit TLS), false for STARTTLS
# SMTP_POOL=false
# SMTP_MAX_CONNECTIONS=5
# SMTP_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# SMTP_IGNORE_TLS=false                # Skip TLS entirely (insecure; local mail catchers only)

# ── Error tracking and analytics ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# SENTRY_DSN=                          # Server-side Sentry DSN; start.sh also injects it into index.html
# ERROR_TRACKING_DSN=                  # Alias for SENTRY_DSN (Env spec name)
# PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=                    # Plausible site domain for the client snippet (default: brand.json domain / APP_URL host)

# ── Secrets: JWT and CSRF ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The admin inbox (/app/contact) uses the SaaS auth stack, so RS256 keys and a
# CSRF secret are needed. start.sh generates EPHEMERAL ones when unset (every
# restart logs everyone out and multi-instance services reject each other's
# tokens) — set real values in production. `npm run generate-keys` creates them.
JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=<generate-with-npm-run-generate-keys>   # Inline PEM with \n escapes ...
JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=<generate-with-npm-run-generate-keys>
# JWT_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=/path/to/private.pem              # ... or file paths instead of inline PEM
# JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE=/path/to/public.pem
# ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL=15m                 # Access token lifetime
CSRF_SECRET=<generate-random-32-char-secret>   # node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"

# ── Storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uploads are not part of the informational front door; the adapter still boots.
# `local` is refused in production unless ALLOW_EPHEMERAL_STORAGE=1 (App Runner
# disks are ephemeral). Provider credentials live in PART 2.
STORAGE_PROVIDER=s3                    # s3 | r2 | local — `local` is DEV ONLY: App Runner storage is ephemeral, uploads vanish on every deploy (production refuses it unless ALLOW_EPHEMERAL_STORAGE=1)
# LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR=./uploads
# MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB=10

# ── Version stamps (set by the build / start.sh, listed for completeness) ────
# VERSION=                             # From /app/VERSION (+short SHA) — shown by /api/health
# GIT_SHA=                             # Commit SHA shown by /api/health
# SPA_HTML_DIR=                        # Directory holding the built index.html (default /app/client/dist)


# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  PART 2 — ADVANCED / SaaS MODULES                                          ║
# ║  Disabled by default for templateType "informational" (brand.json). Turn a ║
# ║  module on in brand.json `modules` before setting its keys.                ║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

# ── Module switches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MODULES_JSON=                        # JSON overriding brand.json `modules` at runtime, e.g. {"teams":true}

# ── Identity shown in emails / API docs ──────────────────────────────────────
# APP_NAME=MyApp                       # Emails, notifications, TOTP issuer (default: brand.json companyName)
# PRODUCT_NAME=MyApp                   # OpenAPI title
# API_VERSION=1                        # OpenAPI version
# SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3001     # API origin when it differs from APP_URL (OAuth callbacks)

# ── Redis (rate-limit store, logout blacklist, BullMQ email queue) ───────────
# Optional: the app degrades gracefully without it (in-memory limits, synchronous sends).
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# ── OAuth sign-in ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Billing: Stripe / Polar ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...        # Server-side only. Publishable key is VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (PART 3)
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...      # Endpoint /api/stripe/webhook
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER=stripe|polar        # Default: stripe when STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is set
# CREDITS_MULTIPLIER=1
# POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Invoicing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# INVOICE_PROVIDER=invoicexpress|console
# INVOICEXPRESS_ACCOUNT=
# INVOICEXPRESS_API_KEY=

# ── Object storage providers (STORAGE_PROVIDER=s3|r2) ────────────────────────
# S3_BUCKET=
# S3_ENDPOINT=                         # Custom endpoint (MinIO, Backblaze, ...)
# CDN_URL=                             # Public base URL for stored files
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=
# R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://pub-xxx.r2.dev

# ── CloudFront signed URLs (lib/@system/AWS/CloudFront) ──────────────────────
# CLOUDFRONT_DOMAIN=                   # dxxxx.cloudfront.net
# CLOUDFRONT_KEY_PAIR_ID=              # Public key id registered in CloudFront
# CLOUDFRONT_PRIVATE_KEY=              # Inline PEM with \n escapes
# CLOUDFRONT_SIGNED_URL_TTL=3600       # Seconds
# CDN_CUSTOM_DOMAIN=                   # Alternate domain name (CNAME) for the distribution
# CDN_GEO_RESTRICTION=                 # Comma-separated ISO country codes to allow

# ── Search ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SEARCH_PROVIDER=algolia|meilisearch  # Default: auto-detect
# ALGOLIA_APP_ID=
# ALGOLIA_API_KEY=                     # Admin key (server-side)
# ALGOLIA_SEARCH_KEY=                  # Search-only key
# MEILISEARCH_HOST=http://localhost:7700
# MEILISEARCH_API_KEY=

# ── Notifications (Slack / Discord) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTIFICATION_PROVIDER=slack|discord|console
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# SLACK_CHANNEL=#alerts
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ── SMS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SMS_PROVIDER=twilio|vonage|console
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM=+15551234567
# VONAGE_API_KEY=
# VONAGE_API_SECRET=
# VONAGE_FROM=

# ── Conversion tracking (server-side pixels) ─────────────────────────────────
# GOOGLE_ADS_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_ADS_CONVERSION_ID=
# FACEBOOK_PIXEL_ID=
# FACEBOOK_SECRET=
# FACEBOOK_ACCESS_TOKEN=               # Facebook Ads Manager (campaign management)
# FACEBOOK_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=
# LINKEDIN_API_SECRET=
# LINKEDIN_CONVERSION_ID=
# LINKEDIN_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=

# ── AI and media generation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=                 # Image generation
# CREATOMATE_API_KEY=                  # Video rendering

# ── Blog: Ghost CMS source ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GHOST_URL=https://yourblog.ghost.io
# GHOST_CONTENT_API_KEY=
# BLOG_SECRET_KEY=                     # Webhook verification secret

# ── Internal endpoints and retention ─────────────────────────────────────────
# EMAIL_TRACKING_SECRET=               # Shared secret for the internal /api/email-logs ingest endpoint
# RAPIDAPI_PROXY_SECRET=               # Validates the RapidAPI proxy header when listed there
# AUDIT_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=90
# GRAPHQL_INTROSPECTION=false          # Dev only

# ── Legacy platform variables (still honoured; remove from any environment) ──
# RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=               # Adds https://<domain> to the CORS allow-list
# RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT=                 # Makes PG* vars override DATABASE_URL
# RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=              # Shown by /api/health when GIT_SHA is unset
# PGHOST=                              # PG* connection parts used when DATABASE_URL is unset
# PGPORT=5432
# PGUSER=
# PGPASSWORD=
# PGDATABASE=


# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  PART 3 — BUILD-TIME AND TOOLING (never needed on the App Runner service)  ║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

# ── Client build (Webpack DefinePlugin exposes VITE_* as import.meta.env) ────
# Read at `npm run build`; the Docker builder stage does not receive them, so
# prefer the runtime injections above (PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN, SENTRY_DSN). Canonical
# home: client/.env.example.
# VITE_APP_URL=                        # Public URL baked into the bundle (falls back to APP_URL injection)
# VITE_API_URL=                        # Leave empty to use same-origin /api
# VITE_APP_VERSION=
# VITE_ERROR_TRACKING_DSN=             # Client Sentry DSN (VITE_SENTRY_DSN is an accepted alias)
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
# VITE_GTM_ID=GTM-XXXXXXX
# VITE_INTERCOM_APP_ID=
# VITE_FACEBOOK_PIXEL=
# ANALYZE=false                        # true = webpack bundle analyzer report

# ── Testing and local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TEST_API_KEY=                        # X-Test-Key header bypasses rate limits (CI smoke only)
# ENABLE_TEST_SEED=false               # true = dev/test seed users and lockout bypass (never in production)
# SEED_PASSWORD=                       # Password for db/seed.js users
# SKIP_CSRF=false                      # true disables CSRF checks (dev only, NEVER in production)
# E2E_PORT=3000                        # scripts/e2e-server.js listen port

# ── Brand ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BRAND_JSON_PATH=                     # Override the repo-root brand.json location (server/src/lib/@system/Brand). Default: walk up from the server tree
